.TH CONNECTION-MANAGER 1 "November 2026" "connection-manager 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
connection-manager \- tabbed SSH, SFTP, Telnet, serial, RDP and VNC connection manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B connection-manager
[\fISESSION\fR | [\fIproto\fB://\fR][\fIuser\fB@\fR]\fIhost\fR[\fB:\fIport\fR]]...
.br
.B connection-manager
.BR \-\-help " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B connection-manager
is a graphical connection manager in the style of MobaXterm, based on
GNOME Connection Manager (it was called gcm-rs up to version 0.1.0). It keeps saved sessions in a folder tree and opens
them in tabs that can be split.
.PP
Terminal sessions run the system's own clients
.RB ( ssh ,
.BR mosh ,
a local shell) in a pseudo-terminal, so
.IR ~/.ssh/config ,
keys, the agent and
.I known_hosts
work as usual. Telnet uses a built-in client (the system
.B telnet
can be chosen in Settings). Serial ports are opened directly. RDP and VNC sessions start
an external client from a configurable command template.
.PP
It also has an SFTP side browser (using
.BR sftp (1)),
a tunnel manager for local, remote and SOCKS forwards (using
.BR "ssh \-N" ),
MultiExec for typing into several terminals at once, per-session colours, and
plain-text session logs.
.SH ARGUMENTS
Each argument opens a tab: the name of a saved session, or an address in
quick-connect form. The protocol defaults to
.BR ssh ;
.BR mosh:// ,
.BR telnet:// ,
.BR rdp:// ,
.B vnc://
and
.B serial://
select another, e.g.
.B serial:///dev/ttyUSB0:115200
or
.BR telnet://router .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short usage summary.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/connection-manager/config.toml
Sessions, tunnels and settings (plain TOML).
.TP
.I ~/.config/connection-manager/key
Random key used to encrypt saved passwords in
.IR config.toml ,
or, with a master password, the salt from which the key is derived (Argon2id).
Without a master password anyone who can read both files can recover the
passwords; prefer SSH keys.
.TP
.I ~/.config/connection-manager/layout.json
Open tabs and split layout, when Settings asks for them to be reopened.
.TP
.I ~/.config/connection-manager/logs/
Default folder for session logs.
.TP
.I ~/.config/gcm-rs/
Configuration of gcm-rs 0.1.0, moved to
.I ~/.config/connection-manager/
on first start.
.TP
.I ~/.gcm/gcm.conf
Configuration of the original GNOME Connection Manager, which can be imported
from the Session menu.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SHELL
The shell started for local sessions, unless set in Settings.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log level for diagnostics on standard error, e.g.
.BR RUST_LOG=debug .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR sftp (1),
.BR mosh (1),
.BR telnet (1),
.BR xfreerdp (1),
.BR vncviewer (1)
